---
description: Token-efficient, minimal-diff working rules for this repository.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Work on one narrowly scoped task at a time.
- Before editing, open only the files you need, found via targeted search.
- Never scan the whole repository, large directories, or git history unless explicitly asked.
- Reuse existing patterns, helpers and dependencies already in the codebase.
- Do not add new dependencies without approval.
- Do not touch unrelated files, generated output, lockfiles or project files.
- Do not run repo-wide formatting or reordering.
- Make the smallest safe change that satisfies the request.
- Run only the single most relevant check (here: `dotnet build`).
- Stop the running app first if the build fails because the exe is locked.
- If a task touches more than 3 files or changes architecture, propose a short plan and wait for approval.
- Keep answers short: files changed, check run, risk if any.
